            "id": "u1-F1",
            "severity": "BLOCKER",
            "file": "calc.js",
            "line": 3,
            "title": "sum skips the first array element",
            "text": "The loop initializer changed from `let i = 0` to `let i = 1`, so `xs[0]` is never added to `total`. Every non-empty input returns the wrong result: `sum([5])` returns 0 instead of 5, and `sum([1, 2, 3])` returns 5 instead of 6. No error is raised, so callers of this exported function would get wrong totals silently. Verified from calc.js:3; the numeric results come from tracing the code by hand, not from running it.",
            "recommendation": "Restore the initializer to `let i = 0` so that every element is summed, and add a regression test covering single-element and multi-element arrays."
          }
        ],
        "attention": null
