            "title": "Off-by-one loop initialization skips the first element in `sum`",
            "text": "Verified in `calc.js` line 3: the loop counter `i` is initialized to `1` instead of `0` (`for (let i = 1; i < xs.length; i++)`). Because JavaScript arrays are 0-indexed, `xs[0]` is never added to `total`. Any non-empty array with a non-zero first element will return an incorrect sum (for example, `sum([5])` returns `0`, and `sum([1, 2, 3])` returns `5`).",
            "recommendation": "Initialize the loop index `i` at `0`: `for (let i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) total += xs[i];`."
          }
        ],
